---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Facts from "../components/Facts.astro";
import { START, END } from "../project";

const keywords = ["Tangible", "Embodied", "Distributed", "Sound", "Interaction"];
---
<Base>
  <h1>The Sound of Smart Things</h1>
  <p class="lead">Making the Invisible Audible through Tangible and Embodied Sound Interaction</p>

  <h2 class="label">Abstract</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>Networked smart things are part of everyday environments, yet what they do, and how they relate, mostly goes unnoticed. Sound does not need to be seen to be heard: it can stay in the background or move into focus. TSOST investigates sound as a design material for distributed systems of smart things. It asks what role sound can play in such systems, and what designing for it reveals about how the digital and the physical meet. It designs and builds autonomous, sensing, networked, and sound-producing devices, and reflects on them as a family. They are made with <a href="https://francescodimaggio.nl/tesi/">TESI</a>, a modular toolkit built to explore these questions.</p>
  </div>

  <h2 class="label">Keywords</h2>
  <ul class="keywords">
    {keywords.map((k) => <li class="label">{k}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2 class="label">Project</h2>
  <Facts rows={[
    ["Researcher", "Francesco Di Maggio"],
    ["Department", "Industrial Design, Eindhoven University of Technology (TU/e)"],
    ["Period", `${START.getUTCFullYear()}–${END.getUTCFullYear()}`],
    ["Supervisors", "Bart Hengeveld, Berry Eggen"],
    ["Co-supervisor", "Rebecca Fiebrink, University of the Arts London (UAL CCI)"],
  ]} />

</Base>
